# Base URL of the auction API that the page is BUILT against — read only
# during `astro build`, to fetch /scene and /leaderboard once at build time
# (the site is statically rendered). In production this can safely be an
# internal, cluster-only address (see infra/README.md) since it's only ever
# fetched from inside the build, never from a visitor's browser. Defaults to
# http://127.0.0.1:3001 when unset.
API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3001

# Base URL of the auction API that the visitor's BROWSER talks to at
# runtime — every fetch inside AuctionFlow.tsx and its children (session
# check, current-round polling, placing a bid, sign-in links). Must always
# be the API's real public origin; an internal cluster address here would
# be unreachable from outside the cluster (see the 2026-09-26 incident this
# comment was added for — an earlier version of this file collapsed both
# URLs into one, and the browser tried to fetch the internal Service
# hostname directly and failed). Defaults to http://127.0.0.1:3001 when
# unset, matching apps/api's local dev port.
PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3001

# Fail the build instead of publishing mock data.
#
# By default, if the API is unreachable, answers with a non-OK status, returns
# a malformed body, or has no champion bootstrapped yet, the build logs a
# warning and renders the mock scene/leaderboard from src/lib/mockData.ts. That
# default exists so `astro dev` and a local `astro build` work with no API and
# no Postgres running.
#
# That is exactly the wrong behaviour for a real deployment: this site claims
# to show who actually paid the most, so quietly shipping nine fabricated
# people as the champion and retinue — because the API was mid-restart during
# a CI build — is a data-integrity failure, not graceful degradation.
#
# Set REQUIRE_LIVE_DATA=true in the deployment/CI pipeline. Every one of those
# fallback conditions then throws and fails the build with a message naming the
# condition that tripped. Only the exact string "true" enables it; unset or any
# other value keeps the warn-and-fall-back default.
# REQUIRE_LIVE_DATA=true

# Stripe publishable key for client-side payment processing.
PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
